Your Card Pack Display Name Goes Here
Starting on this line, each line functions as a black "prompt" card.
As a result, newline characters cannot be part of a card's text.
Traditionally, most prompt cards contain one "blank" to fill in.
These blanks are denoted by adding _ anywhere in the prompt.
You can add as many as you'd like to a prompt.
For example, build a shopping list: _ _ _ _ _
Add ~ anywhere in a prompt to add a random player's name to the text.
There is also rich text support for <i>emphasis</i> and <color=#8000FF>flavour</color>.
After all your prompts have been added, leave one blank line.

Then, on the next line, add the first response card.
Just as with prompts, each subsequent line is interpreted as another response.
Blanks don't have a place in response cards, but you can still use <i>emphasis</i> and include ~ for player names.
Don't include any more blank lines in the file - only the one immediately preceding the first response.
The last line of the file is the last response card in the pack.